27vi|n|To pledge; to hazard on the event of a contest; to stake; to bet, to lay; to wager; as, to wage a dollar. ; To expose one's self to, as a risk; to incur, as a danger; to venture; to hazard. ; To engage in, as a contest, as if by previous gage or pledge; to carry on, as a war. ; To adventure, or lay out, for hire or reward; to hire out. ; To put upon wages; to hire; to employ; to pay wages to. ; To give security for the performance of. ; To bind one's self; to engage. ; That which is staked or ventured; that for which one incurs risk or danger; prize; gage. ; That for which one labors; meed; reward; stipulated payment for service performed; hire; pay; compensation; -- at present generally used in the plural. See Wages.	a:18lq,88,7;ykn,76,2;5p3,40,3;16y3,36,3~18lq,88,7;5p3,40,3;16y3,36,3;ykn,76,2	n:16jb,61,5;5p3,24,1~16jb,61,5;5p3,24,1	N:13tv,15,3~13tv,15,3
