27x9|n|To watch; to observe; to take notice. ; To stay or rest in expectation; to stop or remain stationary till the arrival of some person or event; to rest in patience; to stay; not to depart. ; To stay for; to rest or remain stationary in expectation of; to await; as, to wait orders. ; To attend as a consequence; to follow upon; to accompany; to await. ; To attend on; to accompany; especially, to attend with ceremony or respect. ; To cause to wait; to defer; to postpone; -- said of a meal; as, to wait dinner. ; The act of waiting; a delay; a halt. ; Ambush. ; One who watches; a watchman. ; Hautboys, or oboes, played by town musicians; not used in the singular. ; Musicians who sing or play at night or in the early morning, especially at Christmas time; serenaders; musical watchmen.	a:16r0,0,5~16r0,0,5	V:22bs,18,1~22bs,18,1	n:1dte,13,1~1dte,13,1	N:22bf,66,2;22bs,44,6~22bs,44,6;22bf,66,2
