27zg|n|A small stick; a rod; a verge. ; A staff of authority. ; A rod used by conjurers, diviners, magicians, etc.	a:17fg,128,6~17fg,128,6
27zh|n|To ramble here and there without any certain course or with no definite object in view; to range about; to stroll; to rove; as, to wander over the fields. ; To go away; to depart; to stray off; to deviate; to go astray; as, a writer wanders from his subject. ; To be delirious; not to be under the guidance of reason; to rave; as, the mind wanders. ; To travel over without a certain course; to traverse; to stroll through.	n:19ou,72,5~19ou,72,5	N:1dr4,37,2~1dr4,37,2
