284d|n|One who, or that which, washes. ; A ring of metal, leather, or other material, or a perforated plate, used for various purposes, as around a bolt or screw to form a seat for the head or nut, or around a wagon axle to prevent endwise motion of the hub of the wheel and relieve friction, or in a joint to form a packing, etc. ; A fitting, usually having a plug, applied to a cistern, tub, sink, or the like, and forming the outlet opening. ; The common raccoon. ; Same as Washerwoman, 2.	a:emf,106,3~emf,106,3	n:ec9,108,3;179a,66,4~179a,66,4;ec9,108,3
