2854|a|Full of waste; destructive to property; ruinous; as, wasteful practices or negligence; wasteful expenses. ; Expending, or tending to expend, property, or that which is valuable, in a needless or useless manner; lavish; prodigal; as, a wasteful person; a wasteful disposition. ; Waste; desolate; unoccupied; untilled.	e:1awf,7,1~1awf,7,1
